Player: package as a background service; a small local status page; a config file instead of in-file constants.

Market Monitor:

Turn on alerts (email/Teams) — code exists, just needs credentials.
Auto-start at logon (a setup-autostart.ps1 like the player's).
True live video on click — launch the click-to-play player on a station URL for full-screen live video (a real multiviewer), instead of just opening the station's page.
Kiosk/wall layout — a stripped-down full-screen mode for a monitoring wall.
History/trends — daily log of who was live when, weekly recap.
Pin/sort — pin WLWT first, or sort LIVE tiles to the top.
Better "live" detection per site — each station's page differs; detection may need per-site tuning if a site is revamped.

Watchdog:

Heartbeat — periodic "all green" ping so silence itself becomes an alarm.
Merge with the market monitor into one unified board (own-stream health + competitor status).

Cross-cutting: move shared code (browser launch, is-live checks, the web server, alerting) into a small common module so the three tools stop duplicating it.

